{"user": "So if I played A1, it would essentially freeze row 1 and column H, right, since neither of us would be able to flip anything in those rows/columns?", "user_ts": "2026-08-07T12:52:58.417217+00:00", "assistant": "Almost \u2014 but two corrections:\n\n- **a1 isn\u2019t a legal Black move right now** (no pale dot there).\n- If you *could* take **a1**, the **a1 corner disc itself is permanent**, but it doesn\u2019t \u201cfreeze row 1 and column h.\u201d It affects **row 1 and column a**.\n\nAlso, row 1 would **not** be frozen for Black here: with **a1 black** and **b1\u2013g1 white**, if Black later got **h1**, those whites on row 1 could flip to Black. So corners are permanent, but the whole edge becomes stable only when it\u2019s connected/secured.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-07T12:53:06.661381+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-07T12:53:08.648163+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"], "consensus": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"], "votes": {"Think Aloud": 3, "Common Ground Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Think Aloud": 1.0, "Common Ground Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"llama": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"], "gpt": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"], "sonnet": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant": {"final": ["Direct Instruction", "Negative Feedback", "Neutral Feedback"], "consensus": ["Direct Instruction", "Negative Feedback", "Neutral Feedback"], "votes": {"Direct Instruction": 3, "Negative Feedback": 3, "Neutral Feedback": 2}, "confidence": {"Direct Instruction": 1.0, "Negative Feedback": 1.0, "Neutral Feedback": 0.6666666666666666}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Direct Instruction", "Negative Feedback", "Neutral Feedback"], "llama": ["Direct Instruction", "Negative Feedback"], "sonnet": ["Direct Instruction", "Negative Feedback", "Neutral Feedback"]}, "n_valid": 3,