{"user": "Why do some of these squares not have the white dot that makes them eligible for play?", "user_ts": "2026-08-07T12:53:47.647005+00:00", "assistant": "A square is legal only if placing a Black disc there would **trap at least one straight line of White discs** between the new Black disc and an existing Black disc.\n\nStraight lines can be horizontal, vertical, or diagonal.\n\nExample: **c8** is legal because along the diagonal upward-right you\u2019d have **d7 White, e6 White**, then **f5 Black** \u2014 so those Whites would flip.\n\nA square without a pale dot has no such \u201cWhite(s) in a row ending at Black\u201d line, so Black can\u2019t play there.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-07T12:53:50.653490+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-07T12:53:52.913847+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant": {"final": ["Direct Instruction"], "consensus": ["Direct Instruction"], "votes": {"Direct Instruction": 3, "Provide Correct Answer": 1}, "confidence": {"Direct Instruction": 1.0, "Provide Correct Answer": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Direct Instruction"], "llama": ["Provide Correct Answer", "Direct Instruction"], "sonnet": ["Direct Instruction"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Local Justification", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Local Justification", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Worked Line": 1, "General Principle": 3, "Local Justification": 2}, "confidence": {"Worked Line": 0.3333333333333333, "General Princip