{"user": "Okay, so a move MUST trap at least one opponent disc?", "user_ts": "2026-08-07T12:54:16.381385+00:00", "assistant": "Yes. In Othello, you may only play on an empty square if it **flanks/traps at least one opponent disc** in a straight line \u2014 horizontal, vertical, or diagonal \u2014 with one of your discs on the far end.\n\nThat\u2019s why only **g2, b6, a7, b7, b8, c8** are legal for Black here. If a square doesn\u2019t flip at least one White disc, you can\u2019t play there.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-07T12:54:17.671646+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-07T12:54:19.237220+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Conversational Acknowledgment", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Conversational Acknowledgment", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 3, "Conversational Acknowledgment": 2}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0, "Conversational Acknowledgment": 0.6666666666666666}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Conversational Acknowledgment", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Conversational Acknowledgment", "Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant": {"final": ["Direct Instruction"], "consensus": ["Direct Instruction"], "votes": {"Direct Instruction": 3, "Positive Feedback": 1}, "confidence": {"Direct Instruction": 1.0, "Positive Feedback": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Direct Instruction"], "llama": ["Direct Instruction"], "sonnet": ["Direct Instruction", "Positive Feedback"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Board Report": 3, "General Principle": 3, "Local Justification": 2, "Posi